    ],
    "default": "none"
  }
]
```

### Liquid Implementation:
1. Render custom typography style rules inline on the target HTML element using the `sonu-typography-style` snippet:
   ```html
   <h2 class="typography-{{ section.settings.heading_style | default: 'h2' }}" 
       style="{% render 'sonu-typography-style', preset: section.settings.heading_style, prefix: 'heading_style', settings: section.settings %}">
     {{ section.settings.heading }}
   </h2>
   ```
2. The `sonu-typography-style` snippet will output the corresponding CSS custom variables inline (e.g. `--custom-fs-desktop: 32px; --custom-fs-mobile: 24px; --custom-fw: 400;`), which are dynamically bound to the element by the global `.typography-custom` class in `css-variables.liquid`.

