## 2. Text Highlight Parsing (`[[content]]` & `((content))`)
Always pass text content (especially headings, quotes, and testimonials) through highlight replacement filters to allow custom merchant-defined font highlights in the customizer.

*   `[[text]]`: Wraps the text in a serif/italic highlight class (e.g., `<span class="highlight">` or `<span class="sonu-highlight">` depending on layout context).
*   `((text))`: Wraps the text in secondary highlighted font styling (e.g., Times New Roman italic override `<span class="highlight-times">`).

### Liquid Parsing Examples:
*   Standard: `{{ text_val | replace: '[[', '<span class="highlight">' | replace: ']]', '</span>' }}`
*   Dual styles (e.g. `custom-step-slider-sh.liquid`):
    ```liquid
    assign formatted_heading = section.settings.heading 
      | replace: '[[', '<em class="highlight-pp">' | replace: ']]', '</em>' 
      | replace: '((', '<span class="highlight-times">' | replace: '))', '</span>'
    ```

