## 5. Separation & Isolation of Custom Sections (Theme Upgradability)
To ensure the Shopify base theme can be upgraded seamlessly in the future without overwriting or breaking custom modifications, all custom work must be strictly isolated.

### File Naming Conventions:
*   **Custom Sections**: Append `-sh` (SoundHealth) or prepend `sonu-` or `custom-` to the filenames (e.g., `sections/sonu-v2-testi-sh.liquid`, `sections/custom-comparison-sh.liquid`). Never overwrite a default theme section file directly (e.g., do not modify `sections/slideshow.liquid` to build custom features; copy it to a new file instead).
*   **Custom Assets**: Save all custom JavaScript and CSS rules in separate asset files (e.g., `assets/sonu-v2-testi.js`, `assets/sonu-custom.css`) rather than editing default theme assets (e.g., `assets/theme.js`, `assets/global.js`, or the base stylesheet).
*   **Templates & Snippets**: Suffix custom templates and snippets using the same `-sh` or `sonu-` convention so they stand out clearly during file diffs or updates.

